Third-party attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MLX and mlx-lm (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx, MIT License)

  lily reads MLX's affine 4-bit weight format ({codes, scales, biases}, group-
  wise), and several of its Metal kernels follow constructions from MLX's
  shaders:

    src/kernels/metal/quant.metal   the affine 4-bit dequantization contract
    src/kernels/metal/moe.metal     the sparse-MoE routing semantics, and the
                                    dequant factoring of the quantized GEMV
    src/kernels/metal/gdn.metal     the gated delta step

  The kernels are lily's own implementations for its own tile geometry; the
  algorithmic constructions and the on-disk format are MLX's.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Gated DeltaNet recurrence that tests/support/cpu_ref.rs and
src/kernels/gdn.rs implement, and the online-softmax formulation the
flash-attention prefill kernel uses, are published algorithms; the
implementations here are lily's.
